  "violations": [],
  "extraction_notes": "Single 2025 report for the whole San José Municipal Water System (PWSIDs CA4310019 North San José/Alviso and CA4310020 Evergreen/Edenvale/Coyote Valley); the same PDF is saved under both reports/ directories and this JSON contains only the columns for this PWSID. The one data table is on PDF page 5 (printed as the back inside panel of the brochure) with six source columns, each with Average and Range sub-columns: 'Evergreen (Valley Water Treated Water)', 'Evergreen (Groundwater)', 'Edenvale* (Groundwater)', 'Coyote Valley** (Groundwater)', 'North San José/Alviso (SFPUC Treated Water)', 'North San José/Alviso (Groundwater)'; source_group = column name (asterisks dropped; they refer to the temporary-chlorination footnotes). Cells printed NA (not applicable) have no entry. Lead and Copper are printed once across the Evergreen/Edenvale/Coyote Valley columns and once across the North San José/Alviso columns (90th percentile, number of samples exceeding AL, 2024 customer-tap data). Sample year is 2025 (table titled '2025 Water Quality Data') except footnote a cells (superscript a = distribution system data in 2023) and footnote e lead/copper (2024). Where the Average cell is ND but the Range has a numeric high, value = range high (value_basis 'range_high', average null). MCL/PHG strings are copied as printed including '(4)'/'[4]' (MRDL/MRDLG), '[15]'/'[1300]' (AL) and '(0)' (MCLG). Total Coliform has a blank unit cell and 'Highest %'/'Range' sub-headers; recorded as % with value = highest monthly %. Turbidity appears three times: 'Turbidity (unfiltered sources)' and 'Turbidity (filtered sources)' in the Clarity section (printed as 'Highest Level = x') and a secondary-standard 'Turbidity' row. Anomalies copied as printed: Iron row unit 'ppm' with SMCL 0.3 but SFPUC values 18 / ND - 36 (almost certainly ppb); Potassium North San José/Alviso (Groundwater) average '16' with range 1.4 - 1.8. The report has no violations section; its only compliance statements are 'a reliable water supply that meets or exceeds all drinking water health standards' (p.6) and footnote d 'All filtered water sources met this standard'. Typical-source codes (last column) were not transcribed. This file holds the North San José/Alviso (SFPUC Treated Water) and North San José/Alviso (Groundwater) columns and the North San José/Alviso lead and copper cell. SFPUC HAA5 range high 63 ppb is above the 60 ppb MCL as a single result while the printed average (running average, footnote b) is 42; the report declares no violation."
}
